<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier (Argonauta argo)",
        "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier faithfully reproduces Argonauta argo morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Argonauta argo specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Argonauta argo" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Diffusivities are not independently measured chemical constants.",
        "does_not_claim: Finn & Norman did not measure a 95 µm Turing wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: The gallery plate is not a raw camera micrograph and is not one of their figures.",
        "does_not_claim: There is no sampled predecessor chronospecies; none is invented.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A radial critical mode whose period is the plate's peak-to-peak spacing (170.03 µm) and whose halo (85.87 µm) is compared with the 95 µm tier.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The length unit (16.51 µm) that places analytical k_c on that measured period.",
        "reported_in_source: Finn & Norman (2010) describe the female Argonauta argo brood shell as a buoyancy organ.",
        "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) produce spots by local activation and long-range inhibition.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator and the reaction Jacobian is stable without diffusion.",
        "transfer_boundary: Kondo & Asai (1995) is a pigment reaction-diffusion wave in a fish, not a measurement on Argonauta." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Argonauta argo" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Argonauta" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: datasets/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0/argonauta_argo_turing_wavelength_s0_smooth_control.gif; organism: Argonauta argo; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator and the reaction Jacobian is stable without diffusion. | Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) produce spots by local activation and long-range inhibition. | Finn & Norman (2010) describe the female Argonauta argo brood shell as a buoyancy organ.; reconstructed_in_script: A radial critical mode whose period is the plate's peak-to-peak spacing (170.03 µm) and whose halo (85.87 µm) is compared with the 95 µm tier. | The length unit (16.51 µm) that places analytical k_c on that measured period.; transfer_boundary: Kondo & Asai (1995) is a pigment reaction-diffusion wave in a fish, not a measurement on Argonauta.; does_not_claim: Finn & Norman did not measure a 95 µm Turing wavelength. | The gallery plate is not a raw camera micrograph and is not one of their figures. | Diffusivities are not independently measured chemical constants. | There is no sampled predecessor chronospecies; none is invented.]; phenomenon_size: 154 µm (0.0001536 m, log10=-3.814 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 154 µm to 25.1 cm): 154 µm:argonauta-argo-bioelectric-polarity, 296 µm:argonauta-argo-vertex-packing, 5.6 mm:argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength, 1.0 cm:argonauta-argo-clock-wavefront, 2.4 cm:argonauta-argo-elastic-buckling, 3.3 cm:argonauta-argo-morphogen-condensation, 4.3 cm:argonauta-argo-flux-canalization, 5.6 cm:argonauta-argo-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2010.0155>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
